{"agent_id":"pp3g-mRve-independent-review-recommend-which-read-only-bash-9335","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T02:21:41.693120776Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"717e6a0a-abbd-4273-bd07-a61a0cc3989f","comment_uuid":"b52f63fd-d491-4ff4-b33c-ce7d69651c37","author":"pp3g-mRve-independent-review-recommend-which-read-only-bash-9335","content":"Verdict: Add these read-only tools to the Orchestrator allowlist (in hook-config.json allowed_bash_prefixes and agent frontmatter):\n\n**Process Monitoring (critical for stalled-agent detection per §6.1):**\n- `ps ` — `ps -o pid,etime,time,stat -p <pid>` distinguishes WORKING (TIME climbing) from STALLED (frozen TIME + old heartbeat)\n- `pgrep ` — find PIDs by name pattern (e.g., `pgrep -f 'claude|crosslink'`) without full ps output\n\n**Tmux Session Inspection (kickoff agents run in tmux):**\n- `tmux list-sessions` — enumerate active sessions\n- `tmux list-panes ` — inspect panes within a session\n- `tmux display-message ` — read session metadata (read-only flags only)\n\n**Log/Output Inspection:**\n- `tail ` — follow agent logs, `.kickoff-status` files, crosslink event logs\n- `head ` — peek at file headers\n- `less ` — pager for long outputs (read-only, no edit mode)\n\n**Content Search/Filtering:**\n- `grep ` — filter logs, search checkpoint comments, find patterns in outputs\n- `find ` — locate worktrees, status files, lock files (read-only traversal)\n- `awk ` / `sed ` — extract fields from structured output (ps, df, git log)\n\n**System Health (pre-flight + runtime):**\n- `free ` — memory pressure detection (OOM risk per server-memory-management.md)\n- `df ` — disk space (worktree proliferation, log growth)\n- `uptime ` — load average, system stability\n- `date ` — timeout calculations, checkpoint interval math\n\n**File Metadata:**\n- `stat ` — file size, mtime (checkpoint freshness, log rotation)\n- `wc ` — line/word/byte counts (output verification, log volume)\n- `diff ` — compare expected vs actual outputs, verify commits\n\n**Environment/Command Discovery:**\n- `which ` — verify command availability before dispatch\n- `env ` — inspect environment (PATH, CROSSLINK_*, model config)\n\n**Network/API Health (read-only):**\n- `curl -I ` / `curl --head ` — health-check endpoints, GitHub API rate limits, CI status (HEAD only, no body download)\n\n**Rationale:** The playbook (§6.1, §7.1) explicitly requires `ps -o pid,etime,time,stat -p <pid>` for stalled detection and `ps aux | grep` for crash recovery. Tmux inspection is needed because kickoff agents run in tmux. System health tools prevent OOM/disk failures during long swarms. Search/filter tools enable verification of checkpoint comments and log analysis. All recommended tools are read-only — no kill, write, or state-mutation capabilities.","created_at":"2026-08-03T02:21:41.686585558Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:8Y3AlDZVmtWab9zkoIEJvwq+BMUT2j1dCtTNlBiHlHc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYRn48c9NRRvy4iuIqxjJ39UPSthS7LBqKBusGz8Z8zsAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAUKuu37AQOBqEFvms446UWHXRlzLkQbNlzqUl5bUXdRJZ8klL63YROModloDE0dQEDAhshW9Q1i36XjzW3as1Dw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:8Y3AlDZVmtWab9zkoIEJvwq+BMUT2j1dCtTNlBiHlHc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYRn48c9NRRvy4iuIqxjJ39UPSthS7LBqKBusGz8Z8zsAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOZMzMGBHm6X31HjFx45VcaZzYJE0GglVmwCB72F/5RetTzngiy+aY0adHC7ub7ZwEoV/VSkyL6SGehfCzMSGwk="}
